,title,link,text,language,family
0,Brukdown - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brukdown,"Brukdown is a Kriol mixture of European harmonies (Accordion), African syncopated rhythms and call-and-response format and lyrical elements from the native peoples of the area. In its modern form, brukdown is rural folk music, associated especially with the logging towns of the Belizean interior.",Kriol,Creole
1,Belizean Creole - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belizean_Creole,"Belizean Creole (Bileez Kriol), also known by its endonym Kriol, is an English-based creole language spoken by the Belizean Creole people.",Kriol,Creole
2,"Belizean Kriol (Creole) Folk Songs - YouTubeBelizean Creole People - Music - LiquiSearchKriol Gospel - YouTube MusicThe Music of Belize | Everything you need to know about ...Brukdown - WikipediaStream Kriol music | Listen to songs, albums, playlists for ...Belize Ethnic Groups | Creole | Kriol",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2G6BuMbAGCA,"Jul 24, 2020 · Family singing Belizean folk songs. We didn’t know some of them and they are plenty more that we still don’t know but hopefully you enjoyed watching us and learned a song or two. . Drum-led dancing was a major part of Christmas and other celebrations in Kriol communities. A style of music called Brukdown originated from the all night brams or parties thrown by Kriol families that focuses both on social commentary and hijinks. With the YouTube Music app, enjoy over 100 million songs at your fingertips, plus albums, playlists, remixes, music videos, live performances, covers, and hard-to-find music you can’t get... Developed by the African slaves and their descendants brought to Belize, Kriol music has developed a number of unique genres. One of the most popular styles of Kriol music is known as brukdown (Creole for “breakdown”, referring to “broken down calypso”) that includes a popular sub-genre called buru. Brukdown is a Kriol mixture of European harmonies (Accordion), African syncopated rhythms and call-and-response format and lyrical elements from the native peoples of the area. In its modern form, brukdown is rural folk music, associated especially with the logging towns of the Belizean interior. Play Kriol and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile. They possess a great aptitude to play most musical instruments, but still hold an affinity for those employed by their African ancestors: drums, rattles, sticks knocked together, bottles hit with metal, and grater rubbed with fork. What is Kriol music? Developed by the African slaves and their descendants brought to Belize, Kriol music has developed a number of unique genres. One of the most popular styles of Kriol music is known as brukdown (Creole for “breakdown”, referring to “broken down calypso”) that includes a popular sub-genre called buru. What do creoles do? Most Creoles are engaged in minor manufactures like cabinet making, upholstering and carpentry, trade, construction, and other urban occupations. Many believe in wakes for the dead, obeah, and bush spirits like the DUENDE. They subscribe to a number of proverbs, stories and Anancy tales, handed down to them from the days of the mahogany camps. Who is a creole in Belize? Therefore, in Belize, a Creole is any person who has some African blood, and in a few instances some locally born whites. They are mainly the descendants of the slaves brought to Belize in the Eighteenth and early Nineteenth centuries; of subsequent immigrations of people of African origin; and of the British settlers. What is an example of a creole language? The best example is in the Creole language. The masters taught the slaves the English language; thus, the Belizean Creole became a version of English which has African words, and became the means of expression through which proverbs, sayings, and folktales conveyed African values and wisdom.",Kriol,Creole
